IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `scr-dates`
IMPORT `scr-duties`
IMPORT `scr-process`

-- Supreme Court (General Civil Procedure) Rules 2025 (Vic) -- worked cases for the date helpers (scr-dates.l4) and the
-- party's questions about starting and running a claim (scr-process.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the
-- deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated
-- facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Calendar used: 9 November 2026 is a Monday; 1 December 2026 a Tuesday; 1 January 2027 a Friday; 1 April 2027 a Thursday;
-- 1 June 2027 a Tuesday; 1 June 2028 a Thursday. The Christmas vacation (24 December to 9 January) is 17 days.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Dates and Order 3`

-- Months: same day, or the month's last day (fork F4); back 12 months.
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` (0 MINUS 12) `months after` (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT (`d` 14 11 2026) `is a Saturday or Sunday`
#ASSERT (NOT ((`d` 13 11 2026) `is a Saturday or Sunday`))
#ASSERT (`d` 24 12 2026) `falls between 24 December and 9 January`
#ASSERT (NOT ((`d` 10 1 2027) `falls between 24 December and 9 January`))
-- 14 days after 20 December 2026: 21 to 23 December (3), then 10 to 20 January (11).
#ASSERT `the last counted day of` 14 `days after` (`d` 20 12 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 20 1 2027
-- 3 days before Monday 16 November 2026, weekends not counted: Fri 13, Thu 12, Wed 11.
#ASSERT `the last counted day` 3 `days before` (`d` 16 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 11 11 2026
-- Second business day after Friday 13 November 2026: Mon 16, Tue 17; with a public holiday in between, Wed 18.
#ASSERT `the second business day after` (`d` 13 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 17 11 2026
#ASSERT `the second business day after` (`d` 13 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `d` 18 11 2026

-- Arguments: from, length, unit, vacation counted, public holiday.
-- 30 days from 1 November 2026: 2 November to 1 December (Tuesday).
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 1 11 2026) 30 `days` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 12 2026
-- The same day a public holiday: Wednesday 2 December.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 1 11 2026) 30 `days` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `d` 2 12 2026
-- 30 days from 30 November 2026: 1 to 23 December (23), then 10 to 16 January (7): Saturday 16 January, so Monday 18.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 30 11 2026) 30 `days` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d` 18 1 2027
-- The same with the vacation counted by order: Wednesday 30 December 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 30 11 2026) 30 `days` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `d` 30 12 2026
-- 3 days from Friday 13 November 2026 (5 days or less: weekends out): Mon 16, Tue 17, Wed 18.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 13 11 2026) 3 `days` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d` 18 11 2026
-- One month from 15 March 2026: 15 April 2026 (Wednesday).
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 15 3 2026) 1 `months` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d` 15 4 2026
-- One year from 15 March 2026: 15 March 2027 plus the 17 vacation days: Thursday 1 April 2027 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 15 3 2026) 1 `years` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 4 2027
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period` (`d` 15 3 2026) 1 `years` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `d` 15 3 2027

§§ `Order 1 -- r 1.05`

